  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-emoji-wallet",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-emoji-wallet)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-emoji-wallet)\n[](LICENSE)\n\n> A minimal DeepSeek balance wallet for [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness): one click shows your API balance right in the session header.\n>\n> DSH 余额小钱包：顶栏一个 💰，点一下就知道 DeepSeek API 还剩多少钱。"
    },
    {
      "section": "Features / 功能",
      "text": "- 💰 **One-click balance** — a small wallet button in the session header (right side, next to Session log)\n- 🔒 **Key never leaves the host** — the browser only ever sees the balance numbers; the API key is read from the harness credentials file (`~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml`) on the host\n- 🫧 **Semi-transparent bubble** — click to open, click again to close (auto-closes after 8s)\n- 🎛️ **No config needed** — reads `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` automatically"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install / 安装",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-emoji-wallet\n```\n\nRestart the harness. A 💰 button appears in the session header, right next to\nSession log. Click it to see your balance."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works / 原理",
      "text": "- Host half: `GET /api/wallet/balance` reads `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` from\n  `~/.dsh/.credentials.yaml` and queries `https://api.deepseek.com/user/balance`\n- Client half: a slot component in `conversation.session.header.utilities`\n  (the same container as Session log), positioned before it with flex\n  `order: -1`"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
